course: dictionary
lesson: 2879
title: Doomsday: more than the end of the world
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Doomsday usually means the end of the world, or a day of terrible disaster. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Phones and computers use these same rules to find the weekday of any date, past or future, and the mathematician John Conway invented a trick, the "Doomsday rule", to do it in your head.» Here doomsday is part of a name for a trick. Swap in "the end of the world" and the sentence stops making sense, so this is a different use of the word.
explain: Doomsday can also mean the Day of Judgement, an old name used in church and the Bible. In history, the Domesday Book of 1086 was William the Conqueror's survey of England, and its name is linked to doomsday. Its spelling is different, so look for the e in the middle.
fact: Doomsday means the end of the world, or a day of terrible disaster.
fact: Doomsday is also an old name for the Day of Judgement, when Christians believe God will judge all people.
fact: Till doomsday means for an extremely long time.
fact: The Domesday Book (1086) was William the Conqueror's survey of England, and its name is linked to doomsday.
fact: In a phrase like the "Doomsday rule", the word is a name for a trick, not a disaster. Check by swapping in your meaning.
exercise: «Phones and computers use these same rules to find the weekday of any date, past or future.» What is the "Doomsday rule"? | A list of the worst disasters in history | *A trick for finding the weekday of any date, invented by John Conway | A rule about when the world will end | A rule for counting animals on farms
exercise: Which phrase means for an extremely long time? | Doomsday warnings | Doomsday clock | *Till doomsday
exercise: What was the Domesday Book? | A famous book about dinosaurs | *A survey of England made by William the Conqueror in 1086 | A film about the end of the world | A hat worn by the Normans
test: In films and news, doomsday usually suggests what? | A type of cloud | *Fear of a huge disaster | A happy party with lots of food | A quick snack before school
test: Christians believe that on the Day of Judgement, who will judge all people? | Teachers | Dogs | The Normans | *God
exam: Jayden swaps «the end of the world» into «the Doomsday rule» and the sentence stops making sense. What does this tell him? | It means very old | *It is a name for a trick, not the end of the world | It means the end of the world, so the trick must be dangerous | It is a kind of weather
